k, he went on a trip to Canada and met an incredible Canadian woman who makes him feel alive.\n  - Evan: Evan congratulated Sam on becoming a Weight Watchers coach. Evan shared a picture taken last Friday at a favorite beach spot where he watches waves and sunsets to find peace.\n  - Evan: Evan is excited as his partner is pregnant. He looks forward to parenthood, remembering the joy of his first child, and is planning a family reunion next summer.\n  - Evan: Evan's partner understood his accidental damage to rose bushes. He also enjoys yoga for stress/flexibility and rewatching The Godfather; he previously drank too much with friends.\n  - Evan: Evan is recovering from a knee injury, leading him to do easy exercises instead of intense workouts. He finds this activity therapeutic for self-expression.\n  - Evan: Evan mentioned life throws curveballs, is engrossed in a book, and described a location two hours away as worth the drive for its views and atmosphere.\n  - Evan: Evan's partner was not thrilled but understood an accident involving rose bushes; he was also encouraged by Sam about controlling dreams.\n  - Evan: Evan's partner reacted negatively to an accident with rose bushes; Evan promised caution. Evan was asked about low-impact exercises and finds nature rejuvenating.\n  - Evan: Evan congratulated Sam on becoming a Weight Watchers coach and expressed excitement for Sam's health journey.\n  - someone who gets Evan: Evan's partner is someone who gets Evan, and Evan feels lucky to have found them. Evan and their partner announced their marriage to their extended family.\n  - Evan: Evan's partner understood an accident; he promised future caution. He was asked about low-impact exercises. Evan offered support to Sam.\n  - Evan: Evan's new Prius broke down, causing stress as he relies on it for his active lifestyle and road trips, though he sees it as an opportunity to try new things.\n  - Evan: Evan received a 1968 Kustom K-200A vintage guitar as a gift from a c