aling with various health challenges that affect his confidence and motivation. He has expressed feelings of discomfort that limit his movement and has been experiencing health issues that weigh him down.\n\n3. **Difficulty in Reaching Fitness Goals**: Sam has found it hard to achieve his fitness goals, which adds to his frustration in the journey toward better health.\n\n4. **Maintaining Motivation**: Sam struggles with maintaining motivation, especially when faced with setbacks related to his weight and health.\n\nTo address these challenges, Sam is actively working on several strategies:\n\n- **Dietary Changes**: He is attempting to make changes to his diet, including adopting a more nutritious diet and taking a cooking class to learn healthier meals. This is part of his effort to overcome cravings and improve his eating habits.\n\n- **Seeking Support**: Sam has reached out for help and support from friends like Evan, who encourages him to share updates on his progress and offers motivation.\n\n- **Small Steps**: Sam is focusing on making small changes, as he believes that these can contribute to a healthier life. He has also become a Weight Watchers coach, which not only helps him stay accountable but also allows him to inspire others.\n\n- **Physical Activity**: Sam is trying to incorporate more physical activity into his routine, such as hiking, which he finds enjoyable and beneficial for his mental health.\n\nOverall, while Sam faces significant challenges in his quest for a healthier lifestyle, he is taking proactive steps to address them through dietary changes, seeking support, and focusing on small, manageable goals.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of