any activities, including puzzles, training, and hide-and-seek. Audrey meets with a dog owners group weekly for tips and playdates.\n  - fur babies: Audrey mentioned she has 'fur babies'. Previously, Audrey got a tattoo of her four dogs, and Andrew asked if she was considering getting more.\n  - dog owners group: Audrey joined a dog owners group recently to learn better care for her four dogs and meets with the group weekly for tips and to let the dogs play together.\n  - My dogs: Audrey's dogs enjoy meeting new people. They recently had grooming and look soft and fluffy.\n  - neighbors' dogs: Audrey organized a doggy playdate with the neighbors' dogs, and seeing them wag their tails was sweet.\n  - Pixie: Pixie is one of Audrey's four dogs, a Chihuahua mix, who curls up in her own bed to relax. Audrey is busy giving attention to her four dogs.\n  - vet trip: Audrey took her four dogs to the vet for a check-up, which was chaotic. She plans to take them one by one next time.\n  - other pups: The dogs of Audrey love Fetch and Frisbee and enjoy running around and meeting other pups, who they could keep running with for hours.\n  - the doggos: Audrey takes the doggos for walks in the park to relax and clear her mind, as they offer a nature environment.\n  - puzzles: Audrey's four pups enjoy many activities, including puzzles, training, and hide-and-seek.\n  - pups: Audrey took her pups to the beach over the weekend where they played in the ocean, which she found fun.\n  - Audrey's pups: Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist for her dogs due to abnormal behavior. She also joined a dog owners group to learn better care methods.\n  - city dogs: Audrey's city dogs love trying new parks and trails and go on adventures very often.\n  - everyone: Audrey looks forward to having fun with everyone, noting that her dogs enjoy meeting new people.\n  - Audrey (assistant): Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist last Wednesday for her dogs who were acting abnormally and received tips to help with their problems.\n  - tattoo parlor: Audrey went to the tattoo parlor to get more drawings added to her existing tattoo of her four dogs.\n  - the nature: Andrew enjoyed a refreshing picnic in nature with his girlfriend last Friday. Audrey also likes being in nature and mentioned having a good walk with her dogs.\n  - tattoos: Audrey might get another tattoo when she decides to get another dog.\n  - animals: Andrew acknowledged the peaceful and joyful nature of animals, referencing potential adventures for Audrey's furry buddies.\n  - her pups: One of Audrey's pups pulled so hard on the leash last Friday at the park that it busted; she chased and caught the pup. Audrey calmed her by petting, hugging, and speaking calmly.\n  - pets: Audrey bought dog toys last Monday. Andrew recently adopted a new puppy who is adjusting to his new home and getting along with Toby. Both find joy in pets.\n  - breeder: Audrey got lucky finding a breeder nearby that has the dogs she wanted.\n  - breed: Andrew asked Audrey about her dogs' breed and what they enjoy doing most, following a discussion about dog training and finding dog-friendly spots.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":1984,"context_chars":7486,"retrieval_duration":0.16099905967712402,"response_duration":3.2506484985351562,"total_duration":3.4116475582122803,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer discusses the companionship and joy that Audrey receives from her dogs, which aligns with the gold answer's focus on companionship.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides multiple facts that directly indicate the companionship and happiness Audrey derives from her dogs. Phrases such as 'Audrey's four dogs really make her life brighter,' 'Audrey receives a lot of love and happiness from her dogs,' and 'Dogs bring so much joy to Audrey' clearly convey that the primary benefit Audrey gains from having her dogs is companionship. Therefore, all necessary information to answer the question is present in the context.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["Audrey's four dogs really make her life brighter.","Audrey receives a lot of love and happiness from her dogs.","Dogs bring so much joy to Audrey.","Seeing Audrey's four dogs together makes Audrey so happy.","Audrey feels great happiness because of her dogs."]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_8","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_8_qa_86","category":"4","difficulty":"unknown","query":"What advice did Evan give Sam about finding a passion?","golden_answer":"keep trying new things until something sparks excitement","hypothesis":"Evan advised Sam to try picking up hobbies as a way to de-stress. This suggestion was made on October 14, 2023. Additionally, he encouraged Sam to keep taking things one step at a time, which he mentioned on October 8, 2023.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the event occurred, not the time the event was mentioned in a message.\n\n<FACTS>\n  - Evan suggests that Sam try picking up hobbies as a way to de-stress. (event_time: 2023-10-14T16:07:00Z)\n  - Sam hopes to find something they are as passionate about as Evan is about watercolor painting. (event_time: 2023-05-18T13:47:00Z)\n  - Evan inquired about what hobbies Sam has found. (event_time: 2023-05-18T13:47:00Z)\n  - Evan advises Sam to keep taking things one step at a time. (event_time: 2023-10-08T15:09:00Z)\n  - Evan advised Sam to keep progressing one step at a time. (event_time: 2023-08-15T16:20:00Z)\n  - Evan suggests Sam might find Love in unexpected places by em