down but trying to stay positive. Sam discussed health and rose bush news with Evan.\n  - Evan: Evan is doing easy exercises in physical therapy for a knee injury sustained playing basketball. He misses outdoor adventures.\n  - Sam: Sam took friends on a hiking trip last Friday and is interested in healthy snacks, while also expressing concern for Evan after an accident.\n  - Evan: Evan plans to go on a hike with Sam soon. He recently returned from a morning walk, which he finds helps start the day actively.\n  - Sam: Sam congratulated Evan, enjoys running in the mornings to clear their head, and is dealing with movement-limiting discomfort while trying dietary changes.\n  - Evan: Evan drank too much, had a pee accident near some roses, and apologized to Sam for the embarrassing incident.\n  - Sam: Sam is sticking with a difficult change aimed at living healthier, as discussed with Evan. Sam previously made a yummy grilled dish and is taking a cooking class.\n  - Sam: Sam is trying to keep up with a new health routine despite feeling pressured, and is planning a hike with Evan.\n  - Sam: Sam is dealing with discomfort limiting movement and is attempting dietary changes. Sam previously expressed excitement about being a coach and plans to hike with Evan.\n  - Sam: Sam is aware of Evan's marriage news and offered support. Sam's doctor stated their weight is a serious health risk, prompting plans to eat healthier despite sugary cravings.\n  - Evan: Evan told Sam he is in love at first sight with a woman from Canada and expressed regret for not marrying her sooner.\n  - Evan: Evan mentioned his son had an accident last Tuesday after falling off his bike and is now doing better. He recently finished a contemporary figurative painting emphasizing emotional state.\n  - Evan: Evan told his extended family about his marriage and plans to try poutine in Canada next month. He told Sam he had too much to drink last night and did something regrettable involving roses.\n  - Evan: