ood, where she shared worries and hopes with him.\n  - dog owners group: Audrey joined a dog owners group recently to learn better care for her four dogs and meets with the group weekly for tips and to let the dogs play together.\n  - city dogs: Audrey's city dogs love trying new parks and trails and go on adventures very often.\n  - pet salon: Audrey took her four dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; the dogs were excited, looked cute, and behaved well.\n  - there: Audrey mentioned she'd love to take her dogs to 'there' sometime, following an appointment with an animal behaviorist.\n  - fun outings: Audrey mentioned her dogs had a blast on a road trip to a national park last Friday, enjoying walks near her home park.\n  - gorgeous spot: Audrey inquired about the location of the \"gorgeous spot\" to take her dogs for a stroll.\n  - Audrey's dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; they looked cute with shiny coats and behaved well there.\n  - Audrey: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday, noting they looked cute with shiny coats, behaved well, and were happy and safe.\n  - doggie playdate: Audrey recently organized a doggy playdate with neighbors' dogs, noting the sweet sight of wagging tails, which followed a previous playdate last Friday with her three 3-year-old dogs.\n  - vet trip: Audrey took her four dogs to the vet for a check-up, which was chaotic. She plans to take them one by one next time.\n  - new parks: Audrey's dogs love new parks; Andrew and his girlfriend found a cool park outside the city, which Audrey enjoyed hearing about as she often explores parks with her four dogs.\n  - dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon; they looked cute, groomed, and had shiny coats. Andrew has two dogs, Toby and Buddy. They are considered family members.\n  - four dogs: Audrey cherishes her four dogs, who always make her smile and give love. She has a tattoo of them and recently returned to the tattoo parlor for more drawings on it.\n  - other pups: The dogs of Audrey love Fetch and Frisbee and enjoy running around and meeting other pups, who they could keep running with for hours.\n  - trails: Andrew plans to take both his pets to the trails soon. Audrey previously bought dog toys for her dogs.\n  - neighbors' dogs: Audrey organized a doggy playdate with the neighbors' dogs, and seeing them wag their tails was sweet.\n  - puppies and dogs: Audrey has four doggies that she takes care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be punished.\n  - My dogs: Audrey's dogs enjoy meeting new people. They recently had grooming and look soft and fluffy.\n  - Pixie: Pixie is one of Audrey's four dogs, a Chihuahua mix, who curls up in her own bed to relax. Audrey is busy giving attention to her four dogs.\n  - self-care activity: Audrey does at least one self-care activity daily, like treating herself, while Andrew incorporates coffee breaks and lunch walks for self-care.\n  - Audrey's pups: Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist for her dogs due to abnormal behavior. She also joined a dog owners group to learn better care methods.\n  - tricks: Andrew mentioned that teaching dogs tricks must be super fun and asked how often the walks take place.\n  - Audrey (assistant): Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist last Wednesday for her dogs who were acting abnormally and received tips to help with their problems.\n  - leash: Audrey's pup pulled so hard on the leash last Friday at the park that it busted, prompting a chase until the pup was caught.\n  - pup-friendly: Andrew asked Audrey about plans for making her new place more pup-friendly after the dogs enjoyed the bigger backyard.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2091,"context_chars":7978,"retrieval_duration":0.1905076503753662,"response_duration":4.106945037841797,"total_duration":4.297452688217163,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer indicates th